  'Communication Systems',
  'An analog and digital communications course covering signals, spectra, noise, modulation, sampling, PCM, digital modulation, detection, information theory, coding, multiplexing, and wireless systems.',
  $commsyszzjs${"slug": "communication-systems", "title": "Communication Systems", "description": "An analog and digital communications course covering signals, spectra, noise, modulation, sampling, PCM, digital modulation, detection, information theory, coding, multiplexing, and wireless systems.", "topics": [{"id": "2231039c-4547-4a8c-a190-71272317776d", "type": "topic", "title": "Communication models", "description": "This module establishes communication models as the course's first working framework. It supplies the language and representations needed before the path advances to random signals and noise.", "children": [{"id": "96ea5dd7-a641-4e48-b48d-d165064546c9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Source", "children": [], "description": "Source identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within communication models. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before channel because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "307946ed-c083-411c-90c6-aa8fbf1f8b84", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Channel", "children": [], "description": "Channel identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within communication models. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After source, channel supplies what is needed to address receiver."}, {"id": "cd620086-c4a6-4f2c-82a2-c104edf1790f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Receiver", "children": [], "description": "Receiver identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within communication models. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After channel, receiver supplies what is needed to address spectra."}, {"id": "88f28e01-b734-4c68-adda-7bafcb55ed87", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Spectra", "children": [], "description": "Spectra identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within communication models. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After receiver, spectra supplies what is needed to address power and energy signals."}, {"id": "b2db340b-2bcd-4d31-b64a-25c032f52a39", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Power and energy signals", "children": [], "description": "Power and energy signals is a governing quantity in communication models, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. As the final topic in this module, power and energy signals carries the completed idea into random signals and noise."}]}, {"id": "72912096-477a-4872-9b3f-199b155d1b9e", "type": "topic", "title": "Random signals and noise", "description": "This module builds directly on communication models and develops random signals and noise. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for amplitude modulation.", "children": [{"id": "a7112627-4154-4a6c-84bf-465dc8ff2aa3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Autocorrelation", "children": [], "description": "Autocorrelation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within random signals and noise. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before psd because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "30f380de-e622-4ae3-9018-0ef47d668ae9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "PSD", "children": [], "description": "PSD identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within random signals and noise. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After autocorrelation, psd supplies what is needed to address white and bandlimited noise."}, {"id": "f67a5c26-a474-4208-9ea4-f33b69bc93ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "White and bandlimited noise", "children": [], "description": "White and bandlimited noise makes difficult behavior in random signals and noise tractable while exposing the assumptions and accuracy limits used by later methods. As the final topic in this module, white and bandlimited noise carries the completed idea into amplitude modulation."}]}, {"id": "5bd84e96-37c2-48e5-a231-88b1301c264b", "type": "topic", "title": "Amplitude modulation", "description": "This module builds directly on random signals and noise and develops amplitude modulation. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for angle modulation.", "children": [{"id": "a6d73a03-0d11-4faa-995a-a885b6a24e8a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "DSB-SC", "children": [], "description": "DSB-SC identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within amplitude modulation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before conventional am because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "8500f473-db71-4b96-a925-ef659dbcbaae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conventional AM", "children": [], "description": "Conventional AM identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within amplitude modulation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After dsb-sc, conventional am supplies what is needed to address ssb."}, {"id": "cc7d33f9-b754-4db0-b93c-2f7d4884b8e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "SSB", "children": [], "description": "SSB identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within amplitude modulation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After conventional am, ssb supplies what is needed to address coherent/envelope detection."}, {"id": "b7b5b851-50cd-4473-ad77-483013214d42", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Coherent/envelope detection", "children": [], "description": "Coherent/envelope detection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within amplitude modulation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, coherent/envelope detection carries the completed idea into angle modulation."}]}, {"id": "72c80174-3583-4060-9021-358925fbce2f", "type": "topic", "title": "Angle modulation", "description": "This module builds directly on amplitude modulation and develops angle modulation. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for sampling and quantization.", "children": [{"id": "6efc390c-a7f7-4ae1-b051-3fef2755c2ec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Phase and frequency modulation", "children": [], "description": "Phase and frequency modulation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within angle modulation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before carson’s rule because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "fa7c4d4b-95ca-4578-b73a-66844de2fca9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Carson’s rule", "children": [], "description": "Carson’s rule identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within angle modulation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After phase and frequency modulation, carson’s rule supplies what is needed to address demodulation."}, {"id": "67690a29-9ea2-4745-8da6-3e0bfb2a8981", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demodulation", "children": [], "description": "Demodulation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within angle modulation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, demodulation carries the completed idea into sampling and quantization."}]}, {"id": "29bc6e5f-7a51-44c6-9c30-04f763a8eda6", "type": "topic", "title": "Sampling and quantization", "description": "This module builds directly on angle modulation and develops sampling and quantization. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for baseband transmission.", "children": [{"id": "5bf3ee8a-7cad-41a6-accc-602a6239c049", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nyquist criterion", "children": [], "description": "Nyquist criterion identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within sampling and quantization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before aliasing because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "b22b24e6-d818-43fc-a7b7-e7a3e58cafed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Aliasing", "children": [], "description": "Aliasing identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within sampling and quantization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After nyquist criterion, aliasing supplies what is needed to address pcm."}, {"id": "b439d329-ca8a-438c-9bd3-14942a20776e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "PCM", "children": [], "description": "PCM identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within sampling and quantization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After aliasing, pcm supplies what is needed to address sqnr."}, {"id": "6311c6a7-796d-4b98-9c25-a0619cb9e749", "type": "subtopic", "title": "SQNR", "children": [], "description": "SQNR identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within sampling and quantization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After pcm, sqnr supplies what is needed to address companding."}, {"id": "d1fb9f25-9eb9-4f7f-b22f-7c8f8d13d4ce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Companding", "children": [], "description": "Companding identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within sampling and quantization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, companding carries the completed idea into baseband transmission."}]}, {"id": "106ccd0d-ea3c-4408-93bf-2716367923b7", "type": "topic", "title": "Baseband transmission", "description": "This module builds directly on sampling and quantization and develops baseband transmission. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for digital modulation i.", "children": [{"id": "9db498f9-3e2f-45bc-a7b9-0e4703ffbcfa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pulse shaping", "children": [], "description": "Pulse shaping identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within baseband transmission. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before isi because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "196048f7-45e5-4cff-9acd-5613d31ffcc9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ISI", "children": [], "description": "ISI identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within baseband transmission. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After pulse shaping, isi supplies what is needed to address eye diagrams."}, {"id": "234c5daa-83a0-412e-be78-c2a90ecbddd6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Eye diagrams", "children": [], "description": "Eye diagrams gives baseband transmission a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. After isi, eye diagrams supplies what is needed to address matched filtering."}, {"id": "c5e08e1f-9bd6-47dc-a760-76cf9bfdfc2c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Matched filtering", "children": [], "description": "Matched filtering identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within baseband transmission. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, matched filtering carries the completed idea into digital modulation i."}]}, {"id": "f09a6f43-9c5c-462f-8533-e9271046a992", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital modulation I", "description": "This module builds directly on baseband transmission and develops digital modulation i. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for digital modulation ii.", "children": [{"id": "f0ca626d-5133-45a0-8b36-117c7f5374c7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ASK", "children": [], "description": "ASK identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within digital modulation i. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before fsk because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "98b871f2-e5c3-458c-a866-8fdcad82ca57", "type": "subtopic", "title": "FSK", "children": [], "description": "FSK identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within digital modulation i. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After ask, fsk supplies what is needed to address bpsk/qpsk."}, {"id": "609f4f0e-348c-4145-8fa9-54e56594da73", "type": "subtopic", "title": "BPSK/QPSK", "children": [], "description": "BPSK/QPSK identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within digital modulation i. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After fsk, bpsk/qpsk supplies what is needed to address constellation geometry."}, {"id": "7f8b6b18-696e-4ace-9ac2-9b2d3a3bd193", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Constellation geometry", "children": [], "description": "Constellation geometry identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within digital modulation i. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, constellation geometry carries the completed idea into digital modulation ii."}]}, {"id": "83284490-4f19-4d5b-a5a4-ad25a16364c5", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital modulation II", "description": "This module builds directly on digital modulation i and develops digital modulation ii. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for detection in gaussian noise.", "children": [{"id": "c36b556f-873e-4914-84dc-8847d80d19d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "QAM", "children": [], "description": "QAM identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within digital modulation ii. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before bandwidth efficiency because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "b6ad75d7-463f-4999-9fae-267c25537675", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bandwidth efficiency", "children": [], "description": "Bandwidth efficiency identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within digital modulation ii. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After qam, bandwidth efficiency supplies what is needed to address coherent detection."}, {"id": "998d9e15-0f3c-4455-882a-feece94aef8f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Coherent detection", "children": [], "description": "Coherent detection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within digital modulation ii. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After bandwidth efficiency, coherent detection supplies what is needed to address synchronization."}, {"id": "19e24f97-2ec2-476b-8d75-4c0de9e11d94", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Synchronization", "children": [], "description": "Synchronization identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within digital modulation ii. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, synchronization carries the completed idea into detection in gaussian noise."}]}, {"id": "08d9a8d0-589b-4bc4-899e-52d0652facba", "type": "topic", "title": "Detection in Gaussian noise", "description": "This module builds directly on digital modulation ii and develops detection in gaussian noise. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for channels and link budgets.", "children": [{"id": "ec2cf3a1-ef96-4f57-8a79-c3dc98490627", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Likelihood tests", "children": [], "description": "Likelihood tests is a governing quantity in detection in gaussian noise, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. It appears before decision regions because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "59ff1b58-d27e-44fd-a506-096f48f826ce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Decision regions", "children": [], "description": "Decision regions identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within detection in gaussian noise. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After likelihood tests, decision regions supplies what is needed to address ber derivations."}, {"id": "e3ea2fe5-6162-424c-8ace-b04179462afa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "BER derivations", "children": [], "description": "BER derivations identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within detection in gaussian noise. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, ber derivations carries the completed idea into channels and link budgets."}]}, {"id": "69908551-2fbe-490c-8b1a-285f2f1b9933", "type": "topic", "title": "Channels and link budgets", "description": "This module builds directly on detection in gaussian noise and develops channels and link budgets. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for information and coding.", "children": [{"id": "6978f25e-0e04-4864-b431-21c92e306416", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Path loss", "children": [], "description": "Path loss identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within channels and link budgets. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before fading concepts because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "ab0f65fe-7472-463c-8bc9-008f6ee5723e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fading concepts", "children": [], "description": "Fading concepts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within channels and link budgets. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After path loss, fading concepts supplies what is needed to address snr."}, {"id": "8a2a6023-70d5-45b7-8eb4-3a80dc2c2c08", "type": "subtopic", "title": "SNR", "children": [], "description": "SNR identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within channels and link budgets. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After fading concepts, snr supplies what is needed to address eb/n0."}, {"id": "6345468c-bcd7-42ee-a339-f4cb837d2e23", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Eb/N0", "children": [], "description": "Eb/N0 identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within channels and link budgets. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After snr, eb/n0 supplies what is needed to address margins."}, {"id": "af9efbe8-8972-49cf-b823-0f165fe399ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Margins", "children": [], "description": "Margins identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within channels and link budgets. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, margins carries the completed idea into information and coding."}]}, {"id": "0ca57ba9-9636-4da1-bbbb-cad70ebafe58", "type": "topic", "title": "Information and coding", "description": "This module builds directly on channels and link budgets and develops information and coding. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for system integration.", "children": [{"id": "188533ac-1d9a-42e1-8b18-99e1b8aba6e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Entropy", "children": [], "description": "Entropy is a governing quantity in information and coding, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. It appears before capacity because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "34357e68-cbee-4f55-ae7a-2525983686ee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capacity", "children": [], "description": "Capacity identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within information and coding. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After entropy, capacity supplies what is needed to address block codes."}, {"id": "1636280a-2b88-4edc-b00f-f0b028aa8008", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Block codes", "children": [], "description": "Block codes identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within information and coding. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After capacity, block codes supplies what is needed to address convolutional-code concepts."}, {"id": "692d19cf-86cf-4698-9905-a9f0f3460825", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Convolutional-code concepts", "children": [], "description": "Convolutional-code concepts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within information and coding. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, convolutional-code concepts carries the completed idea into system integration."}]}, {"id": "bfa32e45-ce8b-4857-91e8-a02e1ea6a3e5", "type": "topic", "title": "System integration", "description": "This culminating module draws on information and coding and develops system integration. It belongs last because it requires the earlier tools to be selected, combined, and evaluated rather than used one at a time.", "children": [{"id": "94f77fb4-3cac-4451-a9a1-89010cfbc967", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multiplexing", "children": [], "description": "Multiplexing identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within system integration. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before ofdm concepts because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "eff9a518-f8d9-4133-9df4-06bf61be0598", "type": "subtopic", "title": "OFDM concepts", "children": [], "description": "OFDM concepts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within system integration. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After multiplexing, ofdm concepts supplies what is needed to address trade-space and verification."}, {"id": "05553ce4-23ae-4319-b41d-0a53cac12baa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trade-space and verification", "children": [], "description": "Trade-space and verification gives system integration a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. As the final course topic, trade-space and verification requires ideas from the complete path to be integrated and transferred."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$commsyszzjs$::jsonb,
